---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Nav from '../components/layout/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/layout/Footer.astro';
---
<Base title="Projects" description="Everything built at matterunknown: identity research experiments, and smaller things made for the joy of it.">
<style>
  .head { padding: 56px 0 20px; max-width: 46rem; }
  .head p { color: var(--text-2); font-size: 1.05rem; margin-top: 8px; }
  .cols2 { margin-top: 24px; }
  .prow { padding: 12px 0; }
  .prow .pd { display: block; font-size: .9rem; color: var(--text-3); margin-top: 2px; }
  .status { color: var(--text-3); font-size: .82rem; }
  .shelf { margin-top: 48px; max-width: 46rem; font-size: .9rem; color: var(--text-3); }
  .shelf a { color: var(--teal); text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 3px; }
</style>

<Nav variant="full" active="/projects" />

<main class="wrapb">
  <div class="head">
    <h1 class="statement">Projects</h1>
    <p>Two kinds of work. The research experiments exist to make identity failures visible; the rest exists because building it was fun. Everything listed is real and running unless it says otherwise.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="cols2">
    <div>
      <div class="sc" style="display:block;margin-bottom:12px">Research</div>
      <a class="prow" href="/model"><span class="pt">The Identity Model</span><span class="pd">The framework behind the research: three identity layers, four failure modes.</span></a>
      <a class="prow" href="/projects/identity-map"><span class="pt">Identity Surface Map</span><span class="pd">An interactive map of every system holding a version of you.</span></a>
      <a class="prow" href="/projects/password-graveyard"><span class="pt">The Password Graveyard</span><span class="pd">Enter a password, learn when it died and what killed it.</span></a>
      <a class="prow" href="/projects/digital-shadow"><span class="pt">Your Digital Shadow</span><span class="pd">What data brokers and ad networks probably know about you.</span></a>
      <a class="prow" href="/projects/osint-dashboard"><span class="pt">OSINT Dashboard</span><span class="pd">Identity-research tools, organized by workflow instead of alphabet.</span></a>
      <span class="prow"><span class="pt">agentic-id</span> <span class="status">· in progress</span><span class="pd">Intent tokens for AI agents, built on RFC 8693 and SPIFFE. Will be open source.</span></span>
    </div>
    <div>
      <div class="sc" style="display:block;margin-bottom:12px">For the joy of it</div>
      <a class="prow" href="https://commonlist.matterunknown.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span class="pt">Commonlist</span><span class="pd">One clean address book: connect, clean, and merge contacts across Google, Microsoft, Outlook, and iCloud.</span></a>
      <a class="prow" href="/projects/quant-trading"><span class="pt">Quant scanner</span> <span class="status">· paper trading</span><span class="pd">100 symbols scanned nightly, defensive rotation thesis, every trade public.</span></a>
      <a class="prow" href="/projects/pokemon-model"><span class="pt">Pokémon model</span><span class="pd">17,000+ cards scored daily for mispriced scarcity.</span></a>
      <a class="prow" href="/projects/onepiece-model"><span class="pt">One Piece model</span><span class="pd">The same scoring model, applied to a market with no serious tooling.</span></a>
      <a class="prow" href="/projects/gpk-model"><span class="pt">Garbage Pail Kids model</span><span class="pd">Forty years of a novelty card market, treated like an asset class.</span></a>
      <a class="prow" href="/projects/mtg-decks"><span class="pt">MTG decks</span><span class="pd">Emrakul Commander and Death &amp; Taxes Legacy, built as appreciating assets.</span></a>
      <a class="prow" href="/studio/broken-heart-ohio"><span class="pt">Broken Heart Ohio</span><span class="pd">A tattoo studio's website, booking, and payments, built from scratch.</span></a>
      <span class="prow"><span class="pt">Harvest Haven</span> <span class="status">· building</span><span class="pd">A Roblox farming game built with my 10 year old.</span></span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <p class="shelf">Shelved: Ghost Signal, a five-book espionage series (two books written), waits for the research to have traction. The Vessel experiment is <a href="/archive/vessel">preserved in the archive</a>.</p>
</main>

<Footer />
</Base>
